<% @title = "About" %>
<section class="panel about-panel">
  <h1>About HIVEHUB</h1>
  <p>
    I got into Necromunda with the newest edition of the game, and like every
    fresh-faced juve stumbling into the underhive, I immediately started
    looking for excuses to over-engineer something. HIVEHUB is the result:
    a little tool to make campaign map generation a bit of <em>fun</em> —
    randomly charted hex maps of contested turf, mapped onto the Dominion
    Campaign territories, with just enough grimdark flavour to feel at home
    beneath the hive.
  </p>
  <p>
    The goal is simple: give Arbitrators a quick way to generate, manage and
    print zone maps for their campaign seasons — who holds what, where the
    no-man's-land lies, and which unlucky stretch of pipework your gang calls
    home. If it saves you a whiteboard and a fistful of sticky notes on game
    night, it has done its job. Hopefully it's useful to someone else out
    there in the ash wastes too.
  </p>
  <h2>Suggestions &amp; Bug Reports</h2>
  <p>
    Found a rat in the vents? Got an idea that would make this better? Open
    an issue on the
    <a href="https://github.com/astromoose/hivehub/issues" rel="noopener">GitHub issues page</a>
    — suggestions, bug reports and pull requests are all welcome.
  </p>
  <h2>Elsewhere in the Underhive</h2>
  <p>
    I also write about my descent into the hobby over on my Heresy blog:
    <a href="https://astromoose.neocities.org" rel="noopener">astromoose.neocities.org</a>.
  </p>
</section>
